{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-16566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the center of the ellipse whose equation is\n$4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-16x+2y+13=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-16566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-16x+2y+13 & =0 \\\\ (4{x}^{2}-16x)+({y}^{2}+2y)+13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4{x}^{2}-16x)+({y}^{2}+2y)+13 & =0 \\\\ 4[{x}^{2}-4x]+[{y}^{2}+2y]+13 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}]+[(y+1)^{2}-{(1)}^{2}]+13 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-2)^{2}-4]+[(y+1)^{2}-1]+13 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)^{2}-16+(y+1)^{2}-1+13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-2)^{2}-16+(y+1)^{2}-1+13 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =-13+1+16 \\\\ 4(x-2)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse is centered at $(2,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-16566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b2358ee9a988a6a0375beee19f17e8c95e55560a2ff110e23e30e088182a02a"} {"question" "q-16566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-16566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,1)"] ["math" "(-3,2)"] ["math" "(2,-1)"] ["math" "(2,-3)"] ["math" "(3,-2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-16566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2,-1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine  the lengths of the major and minor axes of the ellipse whose equation is ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-4x+16y=-16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}-4x+16y & =-16 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+(4{y}^{2}+16y) & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-4x)+(4{y}^{2}+16y) & =-16 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+4({y}^{2}+4y) & =-16 \\\\ [(x-2)^{2}-4]+4[(y+2)^{2}-4] & =-16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}-4+4(y+2)^{2}-16 & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}-4+4(y+2)^{2}-16 & =-16 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2} & =-16+16+4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+4(y+2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{1} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2>1,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the length of the minor axis is $2\\cdot 1=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b2358ee9a988a6a0375beee19f17e8c95e55560a2ff110e23e30e088182a02a"} {"question" "q-72934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$2$ and $1$"] ["text" "$4$ and $1$"] ["text" "$4$ and $2$"] ["text" "$8$ and $2$"] ["text" "$8$ and $4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72934" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$4$ and $2$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the center of the ellipse whose equation is $5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+20x-12y=-28.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+20x-12y & =-28 \\\\ (5{x}^{2}+20x)+(2{y}^{2}-12y) & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we must complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5{x}^{2}+20x)+(2{y}^{2}-12y) & =-28 \\\\ 5({x}^{2}+4x)+2({y}^{2}-6y) & =-28 \\\\ 5[(x+2)^{2}-4]+2[(y-3)^{2}-9] & =-28 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}-20+2(y-3)^{2}-18 & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x+2)^{2}-20+2(y-3)^{2}-18 & =-28 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}+2(y-3)^{2} & =-28+20+18 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}+2(y-3)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{5} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72939" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b2358ee9a988a6a0375beee19f17e8c95e55560a2ff110e23e30e088182a02a"} {"question" "q-72939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,-3)"] ["math" "(-2,3)"] ["math" "(-2,5)"] ["math" "(2,3)"] ["math" "(2,5)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-72939" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-2,3)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the ellipse $6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-36x+50y-1=0$ is located at the point$\\,($\n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}-36x+50y-1 & =0 \\\\ (6{x}^{2}-36x)+(5{y}^{2}+50y)-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6{x}^{2}-36x)+(5{y}^{2}+50y)-1 & =0 \\\\ 6[{x}^{2}-6x]+5[{y}^{2}+10y]-1 & =0 \\\\ 6[(x-3)^{2}-{3}^{2}]+5[(y+5)^{2}-{5}^{2}]-1 & =0 \\\\ 6[(x-3)^{2}-9]+5[(y+5)^{2}-25]-1 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-3)^{2}-54+5(y+5)^{2}-125-1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6(x-3)^{2}-54+5(y+5)^{2}-125-1 & =0 \\\\ 6(x-3)^{2}+5(y+5)^{2} & =1+54+125 \\\\ 6(x-3)^{2}+5(y+5)^{2} & =180 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{30}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{36} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{30})^{2}}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-5).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b2358ee9a988a6a0375beee19f17e8c95e55560a2ff110e23e30e088182a02a"} {"question" "q-279724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279724" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279724" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}+72x-100y+19=0$, the length of the major axis is{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must group the $x$ terms and the $y$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}+72x-100y+19 & =0 \\\\ (9{x}^{2}+72x)+(25{y}^{2}-100y)+19 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for both the $x$ and $y$ terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(9{x}^{2}+72x)+(25{y}^{2}-100y)+19 & =0 \\\\ 9[{x}^{2}+8x]+25[{y}^{2}-4y]+19 & =0 \\\\ 9[(x+4)^{2}-{4}^{2}]+25[(y-2)^{2}-{2}^{2}]+19 & =0 \\\\ 9[(x+4)^{2}-16]+25[(y-2)^{2}-4]+19 & =0 \\\\ 9(x+4)^{2}-144+25(y-2)^{2}-100+19 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rearrange the equation into the desired form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x+4)^{2}-144+25(y-2)^{2}-100+19 & =0 \\\\ 9(x+4)^{2}+25(y-2)^{2} & =-19+100+144 \\\\ 9(x+4)^{2}+25(y-2)^{2} & =225 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $5>3,$ the length of the major axis is $2\\cdot 5=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279726" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1b2358ee9a988a6a0375beee19f17e8c95e55560a2ff110e23e30e088182a02a"} {"question" "q-279726" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"} {"question" "q-279726" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14065452/state.json" "file_sha256" "4bc9117ec2842f58026756b3914c9c4b69bb6214376e4afcadb084215aafc28a"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2149 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
